{
  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3747",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to interact with multiple potassium channel subunits through binding, with the specific targets Kcna6, Kcnf1, and Kcnv2 all participating in the same biological process—Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Kcnc2, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Dalfampridine influences potassium channel function. The shared involvement of these subunits in the same pathway implies that Dalfampridine may modulate potassium channel activity through a common mechanism, possibly by altering the functional state of these channels. The evidence supports a role for Dalfampridine in regulating Kcnc2 through its interaction with these potassium channel subunits, highlighting a potential mechanism by which the drug affects potassium channel function and, consequently, cellular electrical activity.",
